  "details": "# Issue:\n\nNormally clicking on UI Buttons in the VRChat Menu plays a sound, this always happens when letting go of your trigger / mouse button.  \n\nThis is however not the case when clicking on the Mute button in the new Here Tab Layout, doing this plays no sound.\n\n**Reproduction Steps:**  \n\n1. Launch VRChat  \n\n2. Go into an Instance with other Users  \n\n3. Open the Quick Menu Here Tab  \n\n4. Click on the Mute button on another user\n\nIf you do this you will notice that no interaction / button audio is playing.\n\n# Expected Behavior:  \n\nClicking the Mute button in the Here Tab should play an interaction sound, just like other UI elements do.\n\n# Attachments:  \n\nHere is a Video showcasing the issue:\n\nhttps://files.catbox.moe/hjdt65.mp4",
